Stamp a current REALITY client version instead of the hardcoded 1.8.2.

REALITY clients write their own version into the first three bytes of the
ClientHello session_id. The server reads it back and compares against
`minClientVer` from its inbound settings (xtls/reality, tls.go):

    if (config.MinClientVer == nil || Value(ClientVer) >= Value(MinClientVer)) && ...

mihomo hardcodes 1.8.2 and offers no setting for it, so every server whose
operator raised `minClient` above that refuses the handshake -- and refuses it
*silently*: the server falls back to proxying the real dest, the client gets a
genuine certificate for the camouflage domain, and reports "REALITY
authentication failed". Nothing in that message hints at a version gate, and
the very same server accepts our bundled Xray without a murmur.

The field is unauthenticated plain text in the ClientHello, so it is not a
security boundary in either direction -- it only tells the server which
revision of the REALITY protocol the client speaks. mihomo's implementation is
current (it handles X25519MLKEM768 and the modern session_id layout), so
declaring the same revision as the Xray we ship beside it is accurate.

Keep this number in step with the bundled libxray.so when the core is updated.

diff --git a/component/tls/reality.go b/component/tls/reality.go
index ff6a0a3..16743af 100644
--- a/component/tls/reality.go
+++ b/component/tls/reality.go
@@ -71,9 +71,12 @@ func GetRealityConn(ctx context.Context, conn net.Conn, fingerprint UClientHello
 		binary.BigEndian.PutUint64(hello.SessionId, uint64(ntp.Now().Unix()))
 
 		copy(hello.SessionId[8:], realityConfig.ShortID[:])
-		hello.SessionId[0] = 1
-		hello.SessionId[1] = 8
-		hello.SessionId[2] = 2
+		// keqdroid: REALITY revision we speak, matching the bundled Xray
+		// (libxray.so 26.7.28). Upstream hardcodes 1.8.2, which servers with
+		// `minClient` set reject as an ancient client.
+		hello.SessionId[0] = 26
+		hello.SessionId[1] = 7
+		hello.SessionId[2] = 28
 
 		//log.Debugln("REALITY hello.sessionId[:16]: %v", hello.SessionId[:16])
 
